# The assessment of AGT-004 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-004: "Nomos shall expose approved capabilities such as semantic rename and
# find-callers rather than encouraging arbitrary shell/regex replacements."
#
# The general principle -- approved, contract-bound capabilities rather than ad hoc text
# scripting -- is real and load-bearing architecture here: `nomos_capability::Registry`
# and `CapabilityContract` are the mechanism, and `nomos-cap-syntax` and `nomos-cap-dependency`
# are two real, tested capabilities built on it.
#
# But the two illustrative capabilities the requirement actually names, semantic rename and
# find-callers, do not exist under any name -- a workspace-wide search finds both phrases
# nowhere in real code, only as this requirement's own canonical text in a spec-ingest test
# fixture. The one real mutation primitive this workspace has, `Edit`, is a whole-file
# before/after text swap, not a semantic operation -- exactly the un-approved, text-level
# shape the requirement contrasts against. And the read-side capability architecture that
# does exist is explicitly capped below what a semantic rename or find-callers would need:
# `nomos-cap-syntax`'s own declared `Ceiling` stops at `FactVariant::Syntactic` and refuses
# a provider claiming semantic name resolution (tested).
verdict: Partial
